;; rules/booklogic/sorts.edn — declare custom sorts for this verifier.
;;
;; FORM SYNTAX:
;;   (defsort :sort-name)
;;
;; A sort is a typed domain identifier. Predicates declared in predicates.edn
;; reference these sort names in their :arg-sorts and :return positions. The
;; primitive sort set {:int :real :bool :string :entity :formula} is always
;; available — you only need defsort for domain-specific kinds.
;;
;; EXAMPLE (commented out — uncomment and edit for your domain):
;; (defsort :solution)
;; (defsort :document)
;; (defsort :chapter)
;;
;; COMMON SILENT FAILURES:
;;   - referencing an undeclared sort in predicates.edn → nbb expand throws
;;     "defpredicate <name>: unknown sort <X>" at compile time (loud).
;;   - typo in sort name (`:Solution` vs `:solution`) → unknown-sort throw.
;;
{:forms []}
